[{:db/id 17592186105825 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-01dbc8f6-a3cd-5172-a886-7310e77fa973" "question-790209a3-d18d-523b-a83b-f000e1032859"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-01dbc8f6-a3cd-5172-a886-7310e77fa973" :question/id #uuid "01dbc8f6-a3cd-5172-a886-7310e77fa973" :question/math-academy-id "q-84756" :question/problem "A student who answers randomly has a $50%$ chance of correctly answering each question on a $12$-question test. What is the probability that the student selects exactly $10$ correct answers? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of correct answers that the student gets.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=12$ questions\n\n- the probability of hitting each question is $p=50%=0.5$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(12,0.5).$ We want to find the probability of getting $x=10$ correct answers.\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=10) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{10})(0.5)^{10}(1-0.5)^{12-10} \\\\  & =\\frac{12!}{10!(12-10)!}(0.5)^{10}(0.5)^{2} \\\\  & =66(0.5)^{10}(0.5)^{2} \\\\  & =0.016\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-304334c9-f645-591e-bc70-9dbb97961017"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-304334c9-f645-591e-bc70-9dbb97961017" :answer-field/id #uuid "304334c9-f645-591e-bc70-9dbb97961017" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-52b8ddff-6335-5004-bb96-e61f512db03c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-52b8ddff-6335-5004-bb96-e61f512db03c" "answer-ddd4b49b-3871-5ead-9a7d-e5c9ef7a0761" "answer-5b2984c7-4c05-5944-a38d-1e1089d0fd33" "answer-b8af0a53-082c-5c70-9f61-4348a58b3949" "answer-ee4df031-007e-5fce-a926-ac3f42667005"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52b8ddff-6335-5004-bb96-e61f512db03c" :answer/id #uuid "52b8ddff-6335-5004-bb96-e61f512db03c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.016" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddd4b49b-3871-5ead-9a7d-e5c9ef7a0761" :answer/id #uuid "ddd4b49b-3871-5ead-9a7d-e5c9ef7a0761" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.056" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b2984c7-4c05-5944-a38d-1e1089d0fd33" :answer/id #uuid "5b2984c7-4c05-5944-a38d-1e1089d0fd33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.091" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8af0a53-082c-5c70-9f61-4348a58b3949" :answer/id #uuid "b8af0a53-082c-5c70-9f61-4348a58b3949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.121" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee4df031-007e-5fce-a926-ac3f42667005" :answer/id #uuid "ee4df031-007e-5fce-a926-ac3f42667005" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.156" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-790209a3-d18d-523b-a83b-f000e1032859" :question/id #uuid "790209a3-d18d-523b-a83b-f000e1032859" :question/math-academy-id "q-130421" :question/problem "Ann has a collection of $20$ pairs of shoes, $12$ of which are sports shoes. Every working day she randomly picks a pair of shoes to go to work, and she has to work for $26$ days next month. What is the probability that she will choose a pair of sports shoes exactly $10$ times? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of times Ann will choose a pair of sports shoes in those $26$ days.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=26$ working days next month\n\n- since there are $12$ pairs of sports shoes out of $20$ pairs in the collection, the probability that she will pick a pair of sports shoes on a given day is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{12}{20}=\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(26,\\frac{3}{5}).$ We want to find the probability of $x=10$ successes.\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=10) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{26}{10}){(\\frac{3}{5})}^{10}{(1-\\frac{3}{5})}^{26-10} \\\\  & =\\frac{26!}{10!(26-10)!}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{10}{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{26!}{10!16!}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{10}{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{16} \\\\  & ≈0.014\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a3d02abe-a662-5d74-8d74-1566af6e8ecc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a3d02abe-a662-5d74-8d74-1566af6e8ecc" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d02abe-a662-5d74-8d74-1566af6e8ecc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7f818466-8ee3-5fe2-9b05-9ed2ed0063a2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7f818466-8ee3-5fe2-9b05-9ed2ed0063a2" "answer-a593bd02-ade6-58ad-8803-fcb266ea11b3" "answer-dba0f373-c7ff-539e-91d7-ee5056b09dda" "answer-985603eb-a536-5f36-917b-88d373887aed" "answer-31d54eb6-7a30-5f6b-bd3e-dc209bc41ee0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f818466-8ee3-5fe2-9b05-9ed2ed0063a2" :answer/id #uuid "7f818466-8ee3-5fe2-9b05-9ed2ed0063a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.014" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a593bd02-ade6-58ad-8803-fcb266ea11b3" :answer/id #uuid "a593bd02-ade6-58ad-8803-fcb266ea11b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.056" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dba0f373-c7ff-539e-91d7-ee5056b09dda" :answer/id #uuid "dba0f373-c7ff-539e-91d7-ee5056b09dda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.091" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-985603eb-a536-5f36-917b-88d373887aed" :answer/id #uuid "985603eb-a536-5f36-917b-88d373887aed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.152" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31d54eb6-7a30-5f6b-bd3e-dc209bc41ee0" :answer/id #uuid "31d54eb6-7a30-5f6b-bd3e-dc209bc41ee0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.157" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105826 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2532926b-6b81-5b1e-a7b4-0b4cbbf77029"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2532926b-6b81-5b1e-a7b4-0b4cbbf77029" :question/id #uuid "2532926b-6b81-5b1e-a7b4-0b4cbbf77029" :question/math-academy-id "q-276040" :question/problem "An unfair coin has an $80%$ chance of landing on heads. The coin is tossed $5$ times. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability that the coin landed on heads at least four times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the coin landed on heads.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=5$ tosses.\n\n- The probability of landing on heads is $p=80%=0.8.$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(5,0.8).$ \n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for the probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x})(0.8)^{x}(1-0.8)^{5-x} \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x})(0.8)^{x}(0.2)^{5-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that the coin landed on heads at least $4$ of the $5$ games. So, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =P(X=4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4})(0.8)^{4}(1-0.8)^{5-4}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{5})(0.8)^{5}(1-0.8)^{5-5} \\\\  & =5(0.8)^{4}(0.2)+1(0.8)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.737,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d29ba2bc-6b0d-55f1-9a0b-b4874a45e108"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d29ba2bc-6b0d-55f1-9a0b-b4874a45e108" :answer-field/id #uuid "d29ba2bc-6b0d-55f1-9a0b-b4874a45e108" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c7a3a7fc-b93c-517e-bc20-23ebc61bbf16" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7a3a7fc-b93c-517e-bc20-23ebc61bbf16"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7a3a7fc-b93c-517e-bc20-23ebc61bbf16" :answer/id #uuid "c7a3a7fc-b93c-517e-bc20-23ebc61bbf16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.737" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105830 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8e763d61-0831-5bdd-b6c6-c5e10a44b471"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8e763d61-0831-5bdd-b6c6-c5e10a44b471" :question/id #uuid "8e763d61-0831-5bdd-b6c6-c5e10a44b471" :question/math-academy-id "q-331639" :question/problem "A wildlife camera detects animals with a $40%$ success rate. The camera is triggered $7$ times during the night. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability that it detects an animal at least $3$ times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the camera successfully detected an animal.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=7$ triggers.\n\n- The probability of detection is $p=40%=0.4.$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(7,0.4).$\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for the probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{x})(0.4)^{x}(1-0.4)^{7-x} \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{x})(0.4)^{x}(0.6)^{7-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability of detecting an animal at least $3$ times. This corresponds to $P(X\\ge 3).$\n\nHowever, computing\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 3)=P(X=3)+P(X=4)+…+P(X=7)\n$$\n\nwill involve many computations, so let's express our answer in terms of the complement instead. By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =1-P(X<3) \\\\  & =1-[P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2)] \\\\  & =1-[(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{0})(0.4)^{0}(0.6)^{7-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{1})(0.4)^{1}(0.6)^{7-1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{2})(0.4)^{2}(0.6)^{7-2}] \\\\  & =1-[(0.6)^{7}+7(0.4)(0.6)^{6}+21(0.4)^{2}(0.6)^{5}] \\\\  & =1-0.419\\,904 \\\\  & ≈0.580,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-723b37c8-0318-5da2-874d-1c31332f782d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-723b37c8-0318-5da2-874d-1c31332f782d" :answer-field/id #uuid "723b37c8-0318-5da2-874d-1c31332f782d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2d415ee2-ce66-5299-b7c3-7e5330a401ce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2d415ee2-ce66-5299-b7c3-7e5330a401ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d415ee2-ce66-5299-b7c3-7e5330a401ce" :answer/id #uuid "2d415ee2-ce66-5299-b7c3-7e5330a401ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.580" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-8e2ae5f5-fad4-5930-b4b2-be1adc26af67" :activity/id #uuid "8e2ae5f5-fad4-5930-b4b2-be1adc26af67" :activity/title "Modeling With the Binomial Distribution" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049632 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-7e04be3f-fd63-5a74-ad92-baa1c03bd6c7" "step-2105619e-8693-5c1a-b9c4-86f38be603c4" "step-29cfbfba-2513-567f-b12d-fc0e4b4fa288" "step-5b5b31f0-1b55-5e0a-8163-ed1fa2d9dca0" "step-63b8acd1-de5d-58b3-b19d-30965be2a286"] :activity/first-step "step-7e04be3f-fd63-5a74-ad92-baa1c03bd6c7" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7e04be3f-fd63-5a74-ad92-baa1c03bd6c7" :step/id #uuid "7e04be3f-fd63-5a74-ad92-baa1c03bd6c7" :step/content "question-01dbc8f6-a3cd-5172-a886-7310e77fa973" :step/next "step-2105619e-8693-5c1a-b9c4-86f38be603c4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2105619e-8693-5c1a-b9c4-86f38be603c4" :step/id #uuid "2105619e-8693-5c1a-b9c4-86f38be603c4" :step/content "question-790209a3-d18d-523b-a83b-f000e1032859" :step/next "step-29cfbfba-2513-567f-b12d-fc0e4b4fa288" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-29cfbfba-2513-567f-b12d-fc0e4b4fa288" :step/id #uuid "29cfbfba-2513-567f-b12d-fc0e4b4fa288" :step/content 17592186265970 :step/next "step-5b5b31f0-1b55-5e0a-8163-ed1fa2d9dca0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5b5b31f0-1b55-5e0a-8163-ed1fa2d9dca0" :step/id #uuid "5b5b31f0-1b55-5e0a-8163-ed1fa2d9dca0" :step/content "question-2532926b-6b81-5b1e-a7b4-0b4cbbf77029" :step/next "step-63b8acd1-de5d-58b3-b19d-30965be2a286" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-63b8acd1-de5d-58b3-b19d-30965be2a286" :step/id #uuid "63b8acd1-de5d-58b3-b19d-30965be2a286" :step/content "question-8e763d61-0831-5bdd-b6c6-c5e10a44b471" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
